            <ArticleTitle>The robotic metroplasty in a patient with hybrid septate variant anomaly.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>271-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s11701-016-0563-2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Complete uterovaginal septum is unusually associated with an obstructed left hemivagina and hemiuteri. Herein we present a case report of &quot;hybrid septate variant&quot; anomaly diagnosed in a 16-year-old girl. The uterine septum could not be completely removed hysteroscopically because of the obstructed vagina and thick uterine septum; therefore an abdominal approach, robotic metroplastic surgery was performed. We propose that the robotic technology has advantages over the classical laparoscopy related with the surgical correction of Müllerian anomaly.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
